            <ArticleTitle>Massive recurrent anterior diaphragmatic hernia, coronary artery disease, and valvular heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1417-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 76-year-old woman found on preoperative evaluation for vaginal prolapse to have coronary artery disease, aortic stenosis, and a large recurrent anterior diaphragmatic hernia. The clinical presentation and surgical management of this case, and the review of the literature are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
